+/// pokezero gen3 fidelity fix: ENCORE is a BOUNDED stochastic duration too, and
+/// upstream never expires it in gen3 — the `volatile_status_durations.encore`
+/// counter exists and is serialized, but the only code that advances it is
+/// `#[cfg]`-gated to gen5+, so a gen3 Encore locks its victim FOREVER.
+///
+/// gen3 overrides the duration explicitly: `data/mods/gen3/moves.ts` gives
+/// `encore.condition.durationCallback() { return this.random(3, 7); }`, uniform
+/// on {3,4,5,6}. Unlike confusion this is Showdown's GENERIC `duration`
+/// machinery, not an `onBeforeMove` counter: `sim/battle.ts` decrements
+/// `handler.state.duration` once per turn during the RESIDUAL phase and calls
+/// `end` when it reaches 0. So the counter burns one tick per TURN — whether or
+/// not the encored Pokemon got to move — and the engine's end-of-turn block is
+/// the same point in the turn, not an approximation of one.
+///
+/// `turns_encored` counts residual ticks already burned, INCLUDING the current
+/// turn's. Conditioned on having survived `n` of them, the chance this was the
+/// last is `P(duration == n | duration >= n)` for `duration ~ Uniform{3,4,5,6}`:
+/// 0 while `n < MIN_ENCORE_TURNS` (a gen3 Encore can never end before its third
+/// tick), then `1 / (1 + MAX_ENCORE_TURNS - n)` — the identical hazard shape
+/// `chance_confusion_ends` and `chance_to_wake_up` already use.
+///
+///   n = 3 -> 1/4   n = 4 -> 1/3   n = 5 -> 1/2   n = 6 -> 1
+///
+/// Exact, not an approximation — the marginal is uniform by construction:
+///
+///   P(3) = 1/4
+///   P(4) = 3/4 * 1/3                 = 1/4
+///   P(5) = 3/4 * 2/3 * 1/2           = 1/4
+///   P(6) = 3/4 * 2/3 * 1/2 * 1       = 1/4
+///
+/// and nothing survives a seventh tick, because the `n >= MAX` arm is forced.
+/// One extra branch per encored turn, and only from the third tick onward,
+/// versus the four-way fan-out a roll-at-application model would need.
+fn chance_encore_ends(turns_encored: i8) -> f32 {
+    if turns_encored < MIN_ENCORE_TURNS {
+        0.0
+    } else if turns_encored >= MAX_ENCORE_TURNS {
+        1.0
+    } else {
+        1.0 / (1 + MAX_ENCORE_TURNS - turns_encored) as f32
+    }
+}
